<topic id="tables">
  <title>Tables</title>
  <shortdesc>Documentation and examples for styling DITA tables with Bootstrap classes.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Tables</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>table</xmlelement></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>row</xmlelement></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>entry</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section id="overview">
      <title>Overview</title>
      <p>Due to the widespread use of <xmlelement>table</xmlelement> elements across third-party widgets like calendars
        and date pickers, Bootstrap’s tables are opt-in. Extend with optional modifier output classes or custom styles.
        All table styles are not inherited in Bootstrap, meaning any nested tables can be styled independent from the
        parent.</p>
      <p>Using the most basic table markup, here’s how the default DITA Bootstrap <codeph>.table</codeph>-based tables
        look in Bootstrap.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>

    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/overview.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="variants">
      <title>Variants</title>
      <p>Use contextual classes to color tables, table rows or individual cells.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="p-1 w-100 theme-primary">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row outputclass="theme-info">
              <entry>Elephant (African and Asian)</entry>
              <entry>Loxodonta africana, Elephas maximus</entry>
              <entry>19-22 months</entry>
            </row>
            <row outputclass="theme-success">
              <entry>Giraffe</entry>
              <entry>Giraffa camelopardalis</entry>
              <entry>15 months</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>Rhinoceros</entry>
              <entry>Rhinocerotidae</entry>
              <entry outputclass="theme-danger">14-16 months</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>Hippopotamus</entry>
              <entry>Hippopotamus amphibius</entry>
              <entry>7 1/2 months</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>

    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/variants.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="striped-rows">
      <title>Striped rows</title>
      <p>Use <xmlatt>striped="yes"</xmlatt> to add zebra-striping to any table row
        within the <xmlelement>tbody</xmlelement>.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="table-striped">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/striped-rows.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="striped-columns">
      <title>Striped columns</title>
      <p>Use <xmlatt>striped-columns="yes"</xmlatt> to add zebra-striping to any table column
        within the <xmlelement>tbody</xmlelement>.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="table-striped-columns">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/striped-columns.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="bordered-tables">
      <title>Bordered tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>rowsep="1"</xmlatt> and <xmlatt
        >colsep="1"</xmlatt> for borders on all sides of the table and cells.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table rowsep="1" colsep="1">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/bordered-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="tables-without-borders">
      <title>Tables without borders</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>rowsep="0"</xmlatt> and <xmlatt>colsep="0"</xmlatt> for a table without borders.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table rowsep="0" colsep="0">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/tables-without-borders.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="small-tables">
      <title>Small tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>outputclass="table-sm"</xmlatt> to make any table more compact by cutting all cell <codeph
        >padding</codeph> in half.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="table-sm">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/small-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="table-group-dividers">
      <title>Table group dividers</title>
      <p>Add a thicker border, darker between table groups—<xmlelement>thead</xmlelement> and <xmlelement
        >tbody</xmlelement>, with <xmlatt>divider="yes"</xmlatt> on the table.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody outputclass="table-group-divider" conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/table-group-dividers.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="vertical-alignment">
      <title>Vertical alignment</title>
      <p>Table cells of <xmlelement
        >thead</xmlelement> are always vertical aligned to the bottom. Table cells in <xmlelement
        >tbody</xmlelement> inherit their alignment from <xmlelement
        >table</xmlelement> and are aligned to the top by default. Use the <xmlatt
        >valign</xmlatt> attribute to re-align where needed.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="align-middle">
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC3"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry colname="COLSPEC0" valign="top">Heading 1</entry>
              <entry colname="COLSPEC1" valign="bottom">Heading 2</entry>
              <entry colname="COLSPEC2" valign="middle">Heading 3</entry>
              <entry
                colname="COLSPEC3"
              >Heading 4 - here is some placeholder text, intended to take up quite a bit of vertical space, to demonstrate how the vertical alignment works in the headers</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>

          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>outputclass="align-middle"</xmlatt> from the table</entry>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>outputclass="align-middle"</xmlatt> from the table</entry>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>outputclass="align-middle"</xmlatt> from the table</entry>
              <entry
              >This here is some placeholder text, intended to take up quite a bit of vertical space, to demonstrate how the vertical alignment works in the preceding cells.</entry>
            </row>
            <row valign="bottom">
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>valign="bottom"</xmlatt> from the table row</entry>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>valign="bottom"</xmlatt> from the table row</entry>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>valign="bottom"</xmlatt> from the table row</entry>
              <entry
              >This here is some placeholder text, intended to take up quite a bit of vertical space, to demonstrate how the vertical alignment works in the preceding cells.</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>outputclass="align-middle"</xmlatt> from the table</entry>
              <entry>This cell inherits <xmlatt>outputclass="align-middle"</xmlatt> from the table</entry>
              <entry valign="top">This cell is aligned to the top.</entry>
              <entry
              >This here is some placeholder text, intended to take up quite a bit of vertical space, to demonstrate how the vertical alignment works in the preceding cells.</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/vertical-alignment.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="table-head">
      <title>Table head</title>
      <p>Similar to tables and dark tables, use the modifier <xmlatt>theme="secondary"</xmlatt> or
          <xmlatt>theme="inverse"</xmlatt> to make <xmlelement>thead</xmlelement> elements appear light or dark
        gray.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead outputclass="theme-secondary" conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/table-head.xml"/></codeblock>
    <example>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC0"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC1"/>
          <colspec colname="COLSPEC2"/>
          <thead outputclass="theme-inverse" conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/table-head-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="card-like-tables">
      <title>Card-like tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>outputclass="table-card"</xmlatt> to a table to round the corners like a card.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="table-striped table-card">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colname="c3"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/card-like-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="table-footer">
      <title>Footer</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>outputclass="tfoot"</xmlatt> to a <xmlelement>row</xmlelement> of the <xmlelement>tbody</xmlelement> to move it into a table footer row group, and <xmlatt>outputclass="thead"</xmlatt> to an <xmlelement>entry</xmlelement> to render it as a row header.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table>
        <title>Monthly Sales Report</title>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="col1" colnum="1"/>
          <colspec colname="col2" colnum="2"/>
          <colspec colname="col3" colnum="3"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Product</entry>
              <entry>Units Sold</entry>
              <entry>Revenue</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry outputclass="thead">Product A</entry>
              <entry>100</entry>
              <entry>$1,000</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry outputclass="thead">Product B</entry>
              <entry>150</entry>
              <entry>$1,500</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry outputclass="thead">Product C</entry>
              <entry>250</entry>
              <entry>$2,500</entry>
            </row>
            <row outputclass="tfoot">
              <entry>Total</entry>
              <entry>500</entry>
              <entry>$5,000</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/table-footer.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="caption">
      <title>Caption</title>
      <p>A table <xmlelement>title</xmlelement> renders as the caption, below the table by default. Add <xmlatt>outputclass="caption-top"</xmlatt> to move it above.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="caption-top">
        <title>List of animals</title>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colname="c3"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/caption.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="stacked-tables">
      <title>Stacked tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>outputclass="md:table-stacked"</xmlatt> to a table to collapse rows into stacked label and value pairs below a container breakpoint. Use <xmlatt>outputclass="table-stacked"</xmlatt> to always stack. Each cell is labelled with its column heading, and the required responsive wrapper is generated automatically.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="md:table-stacked">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colname="c3"/>
          <thead conref="animals.dita#animals/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="animals.dita#animals/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/stacked-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
    <section id="responsive-tables">
      <title>Responsive tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>outputclass="table-responsive"</xmlatt> to a table to scroll horizontally, or use <codeph>sm:</codeph> to <codeph>2xl:</codeph> prefixed variants such as <xmlatt>outputclass="xl:table-responsive"</xmlatt> to scroll only below a breakpoint. The scrolling wrapper is generated automatically.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <table outputclass="xl:table-responsive">
        <tgroup cols="12">
          <colspec colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colname="c3"/>
          <colspec colname="c4"/>
          <colspec colname="c5"/>
          <colspec colname="c6"/>
          <colspec colname="c7"/>
          <colspec colname="c8"/>
          <colspec colname="c9"/>
          <colspec colname="c10"/>
          <colspec colname="c11"/>
          <colspec colname="c12"/>
          <thead conref="wide-table.dita#wide-table/head">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody conref="wide-table.dita#wide-table/data">
            <row><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </example>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/tables/responsive-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
  </body>
</topic>
